3. Export ProcessedAtNanosKey so callers can inject it optionally.
4. Update ticker.go to pass app ctx instead of context.Background()."

Description:
GOROUTINE LEAK. internal/realtime/hub.go ServeHeatmap launches:
  go func() {
      for { if _, _, err := conn.ReadMessage(); err != nil { return } }
  }()

This drain goroutine has no context, no stop signal. If the outer ServeHeatmap handler returns (e.g., ctx.Done() fires) but the connection is not yet closed, the drain goroutine blocks indefinitely on ReadMessage.

FIX:
  go func() {
      for {
          if _, _, err := conn.ReadMessage(); err != nil {
              return
          }
          select {
          case <-ctx.Done(): return
          default:
          }
      }
  }()

Also: ensure conn.Close() is called in the deferred cleanup and that heatmapClients.Delete(conn) runs even if the goroutine panics.

LOCK CONTENTION. InProcessTickBus.Publish holds mu.RLock() for the entire publish loop. Any concurrent Subscribe() call that needs mu.Lock() is blocked for the duration of all channel sends.

Under 10 instruments × 8x sim = 80 publishes/sec × 2 subscribers, the lock is held almost continuously, starving new subscribers.

FIX:
  func (b *InProcessTickBus) Publish(...) error {
      b.mu.RLock()
      subs := make([]chan NormalizedTick, len(b.subscribers))
      copy(subs, b.subscribers)
      b.mu.RUnlock()  // release before channel ops
      for _, ch := range subs {
          select {
          case ch <- tick:
          default: atomic.AddUint64(&b.droppedTicks, 1)
          }
      }
      return nil
  }

F&O margin requirements differ significantly from equity.

MARGIN CALCULATION (internal/paper/margin.go):

  type MarginRequirement struct {
      SPAN        float64  // SPAN margin (worst-case scenario)
      Exposure    float64  // Exchange exposure margin
      Total       float64  // SPAN + Exposure
      Available   float64  // cash - Total
  }

  // Simplified SPAN (actual SPAN is complex; use NSE margin calculator as reference)
  func EstimateSPAN(position PaperPosition, vix float64) float64 {
      // For futures: lot_size * CMP * margin_pct (≈10-15% for index futures)
      // For long options: just the premium paid (defined risk)
      // For short options: SPAN = lot_size * CMP * vix_based_multiplier
  }

P&L CALCULATION:
  - Unrealized P&L: (CMP - AvgPrice) * Qty * LotSize
  - For short options: (AvgPrice - CMP) * Qty * LotSize
  - MTM P&L: end-of-day settlement at exchange closing price
  - Include brokerage simulation: ₹20 per order (Zerodha flat fee) + STT + SEBI charges + stamp duty

  type TradeCharges struct {
      Brokerage   float64  // ₹20 flat
      STT         float64  // 0.01% sell-side for options
      SEBI        float64  // ₹10/crore
      StampDuty   float64  // 0.003% buy-side
      Total       float64
  }
  func ComputeCharges(orderValue float64, txType string) TradeCharges

REST ENDPOINT:
  GET /api/v1/paper/margin — current margin utilization
  GET /api/v1/paper/pnl   — P&L summary with charges breakdown

TRADING SAFETY. A Global Kill Switch is mandatory before any paper or live trading. It must be able to halt all order activity instantly.

IMPLEMENTATION (internal/safety/killswitch.go):

  var globalKillSwitch int32  // 0=active, 1=halted; atomic

  func IsHalted() bool {
      return atomic.LoadInt32(&globalKillSwitch) == 1
  }
  func Halt(reason string) {
      atomic.StoreInt32(&globalKillSwitch, 1)
      zap.L().Error(\GLOBAL KILL SWITCH ACTIVATED"

